    <statement><p>For the following indefinite integral, find the full power series centered at <m>t=0</m> and then give the first 5 nonzero terms of the power series and the open interval of convergence.</p>
<p><me>f(t) = \int \frac{t}{1+t^{9}}\ dt</me></p>
<p><m>f(t) = C + \displaystyle\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f(t) = C +</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>+ \cdots</m></p>
<p>The open interval of convergence is: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0007"/> (Give your answer in .)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(-1\right)^{n}t^{9n+2}}{9n+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{t^{9\cdot 0+2}}{9\cdot 0+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1t^{9\cdot 1+2}}{9\cdot 1+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{t^{9\cdot 2+2}}{9\cdot 2+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1t^{9\cdot 3+2}}{9\cdot 3+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{t^{9\cdot 4+2}}{9\cdot 4+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-1,1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
